From 26d10f223d34b7b9a89170a374ab4d671132b683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akshat Srivastava <akshat.sanya@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Roles, playable Dungeon Master, artwork, hosting on a server

Networking
- Menu: host on this computer or on a server address (dedicated dungeon_server),
  so rooms can be played across networks when that server is reachable
- Lobby shows this computer's local address when hosting locally
- Help popup explaining hosting options

Roles / Dungeon Master
- Lobby role choice is sent to the server; only one DM per room
- Human DM: order monsters (card -> monster -> hero) and the final boss; attacks run on End turn
- Computer DM now attacks (each monster hits the weakest hero, boss too)
- Final boss from the level file is configured and arrives in its round
- Healer hero, Heal card (played on heroes), Monster Attack DM card, DM deck in level_1
  (all placeholder values marked temporary - confirm with Irma)

Artwork
- Menu background, Help button, card artwork (+ empty card design fallback),
  Healer/boss artwork, Heroes_Win/Heroes_Lose game-over screen
- Fix: widgets used the name as ImGui ID, so two Goblins / two Strike cards merged into one

Data loader
- Optional card "image" and level "dungeonMaster" { maxMana, startingDeck }

Tests
- net_tests: roles, DM uniqueness, DM commands damage the chosen hero, computer DM attacks, boss arrival
